      "body_html": "I went over to visit my friend Drew Martinez with another homie, Rob Co, and we were blown away by his nepenthes collection!  When I visited Drew's collection last year, and it was pretty amazing, but I have to say hats off for what it looks like right now!  Thanks Drew for letting us check out your collection!<br/><br/>  His nepenthes collection is like a library of species and hybrids all thriving in his overly packed greenhouse-enjoy the photos:<br/><br/><br/><br/>N. hamata-a really nice clone:<br/><img src=\"http://i1110.photobucket.com/albums/h443/meizzwang/n12.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/><br/><br/><br/>N. hamata-a different clone:<br/><img src=\"http://i1110.photobucket.com/albums/h443/meizzwang/n13.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/><br/><br/><br/><br/>N. arostolochioides:<br/><img src=\"http://i1110.photobucket.com/albums/h443/meizzwang/h5-1.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/><br/><br/>closer view:<br/><img src=\"http://i1110.photobucket.com/albums/h443/meizzwang/h4-2.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/><br/><br/><br/>N. platychila:<br/><img src=\"http://i1110.photobucket.com/albums/h443/meizzwang/n26.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/><br/><br/><br/>N. inermis<br/><img src=\"http://i1110.photobucket.com/albums/h443/meizzwang/n24.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/><br/><br/><br/>N. sanguinea:<br/><img src=\"http://i1110.photobucket.com/albums/h443/meizzwang/n23.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/><br/><br/>N. sanguinea:<br/><img src=\"http://i1110.photobucket.com/albums/h443/meizzwang/n22.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/><br/><br/><img src=\"http://i1110.photobucket.com/albums/h443/meizzwang/n14.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/><br/><br/>N. vogelii:<br/><img src=\"http://i1110.photobucket.com/albums/h443/meizzwang/n31.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/><br/><br/>N. vogelii:<br/><img src=\"http://i1110.photobucket.com/albums/h443/meizzwang/n32.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/><br/><br/><br/>N. vogelii:<br/><img src=\"http://i1110.photobucket.com/albums/h443/meizzwang/n40.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/><br/><br/><br/>N. ephippiata:<br/><img src=\"http://i1110.photobucket.com/albums/h443/meizzwang/n29.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/><br/><br/>N. ephippiata:<br/><img src=\"http://i1110.photobucket.com/albums/h443/meizzwang/n28.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/><br/><br/><br/>N. lowii lower pitcher:<br/><img src=\"http://i1110.photobucket.com/albums/h443/meizzwang/n42.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/><br/><br/><br/>N. x Tivyei (I think):<br/><img src=\"http://i1110.photobucket.com/albums/h443/meizzwang/n19.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/>]<br/><br/><br/>Nepenthes hybrid:<br/><img src=\"http://i1110.photobucket.com/albums/h443/meizzwang/n21.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/><br/><br/><img src=\"http://i1110.photobucket.com/albums/h443/meizzwang/n18.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/><br/><br/><br/><br/>N. queen of hearts x king of spades:<br/><img src=\"http://i1110.photobucket.com/albums/h443/meizzwang/n36.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/><br/><br/>Can't remember what this is,but I'm sure one of you out there do:<br/><img src=\"http://i1110.photobucket.com/albums/h443/meizzwang/n38.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/><br/><br/><br/>Some nice healthy seedlings:<br/><img src=\"http://i1110.photobucket.com/albums/h443/meizzwang/n33.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/><br/><br/>Hundreds of different clones in his collection:<br/><img src=\"http://i1110.photobucket.com/albums/h443/meizzwang/n5-1.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/><br/><br/><br/><img src=\"http://i1110.photobucket.com/albums/h443/meizzwang/n7.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/><br/><br/><img src=\"http://i1110.photobucket.com/albums/h443/meizzwang/n8.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/><br/><br/><img src=\"http://i1110.photobucket.com/albums/h443/meizzwang/n9.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/><br/><br/><img src=\"http://i1110.photobucket.com/albums/h443/meizzwang/n10.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/><br/><br/><img src=\"http://i1110.photobucket.com/albums/h443/meizzwang/n11.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/><br/><br/><br/>and last but not least, the grower of all these amazing plants, Drew Martinez, with his well grown specimen:<br/><img src=\"http://i1110.photobucket.com/albums/h443/meizzwang/N3-1.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/><br/><br/><br/>",
